CORE
main.c
--refine-concurrency
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
All reads of an object within an atomic section, on any branch, see the value
the object has when the section starts: the read of flag implies that the
writer's atomic section precedes the reader's one, and so both reads of buf
(on different branches) see the value written.
As test.desc, with the from-read constraints added lazily (--refine-concurrency).
